@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "zendesk.integration"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Non Integration
	Testing updates that should not be present in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB.

Setup:
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I create an account on koroneiki with the following values
	| Code     | OSBZENOSBZEN                  | |
	| Language | English                       | |
	| Name     | Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} | |
	| Region   | United States                 | |
	| Status   | Active                        | |
	| Tier     | T1                            | |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	* I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Watcher |
	Then the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes via groovy
	| OSBZENOSBZEN |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Osbzen - ${staticProjectName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View no project and user sync after role updates
	Customer role updates should not be reflected in Zendesk if customers and their respective organizations are not part of Zendesk.

	Given I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Watcher |
	And I assign the contact with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| Support Developer |
	And I remove the contact with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" from the following roles	
	| Support Developer |
	And I remove the contact with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" on the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" from the following roles	
	| Support Watcher |
	Then the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View no project and user sync after customer removal
	Customer removal updates should not be reflected in Zendesk if customers and their respective organizations are not part of Zendesk.

	Given I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	Then the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View no project and user sync after watcher removal
	Watcher removal updates should not be reflected in Zendesk if customers and their respective organizations are not part of Zendesk.

	Given I remove customer contacts with the following email addresses from the account "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}"
	| osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	Then the organization "Osbzen - ${staticProjectName}" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" should not be present on zendesk.liferay.com